WEBVTT

00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:03.790
Playmaker!

00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:05.050
You're okay.

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:09.490
Seems you defeated Go Onizuka.

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:13.230
Of course.  Because I was with him.

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:15.330
You're one to talk.

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:17.630
Now no one will interfere.

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:19.070
Let's hurry!

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:25.830
What is this place?

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:28.540
Is our target still further ahead?

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:35.830
Is that the gate?

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:38.480
He must've gone through that.

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:41.880
Let's go!

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:57.870
Is Playmaker further ahead?

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:01.110
They probably went through that gate already.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:03.710
We're going too!

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:12.560
There they go.

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:15.960
Aoi, come home safe.

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:38.290
Our lives aren't forever

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:45.100
We wander, searching for the meaning of life

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:52.380
Even if it's not the right direction, just keep looking forward

00:01:52.870 --> 00:01:58.950
Sharing hope for the future

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:05.720
tell me  We're searching for memories lost in the darkness

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:12.960
I feel your flame  Your impulses pierce the light

00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:19.640
I want to share your pain

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:53.750
How far does this go?

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:54.950
Are we safe?

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:56.720
We can't go back anymore.

00:02:56.940 --> 00:03:00.090
Exactly.  You'll understand when we get there.

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:04.530
Is the exit near?

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:16.220
This wind is dangerous!

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:17.250
Are you scared?

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:18.040
I'm fine!

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:25.090
Stay focused.  If you crash into the cliff, you'll be hurt!

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:26.280
I know!

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:29.960
Be careful!

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:52.780
I'm releasing you!

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:53.610
Okay!

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:08.610
Are you okay?

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:10.630
Thank you for saving me.

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:15.370
This wind must've put the research team in distress.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:18.740
We lost sight of Playmaker.

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:23.620
What should we do?

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:26.680
Or we'll be in distress too.

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:33.290
This call sign is...

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:35.460
The research team's emergency signal.

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:36.560
We have to save them!

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:37.390
Hey!

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:41.340
Sheesh!  I'm adding extra for special care!

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:47.470
The Ignis's program territory is ahead.

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:50.100
No one know what'll happen.

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:52.940
I'm counting on you, Yusaku and Takeru.

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:58.180
The Ignis program is a unique algorithm that Dr. Kogami developed.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:02.150
If I can't solve it, I can't help at all.

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:04.020
I promise to solve it!

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:11.920
It's only a matter of time until we fall!

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:14.890
Flame!  It's up to us!

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:16.800
Seems so.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:22.800
I'm bracing so hard that I'm about to fart.

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:24.870
We don't have that function.

00:05:25.530 --> 00:05:28.280
Use the Data Storm to negate the wind...

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:30.130
I see.  That's a good idea.

00:05:30.130 --> 00:05:32.850
Right?  Praise me more!

00:05:58.110 --> 00:06:00.610
They're close by.

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:04.530
Yes.  But with this wind...

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:13.320
Hey!

00:06:17.830 --> 00:06:20.160
A cave!  They're there!

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:32.770
The wind made them fall.

00:06:32.770 --> 00:06:36.300
You can't log out normally from here.

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:39.250
And the emergency signal didn't reach the outside.

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:43.950
Let's leave.

00:06:44.310 --> 00:06:46.170
They can still be saved.

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:50.310
Hold up!  That emergency evac program is-

00:06:50.310 --> 00:06:54.360
I know!  If we use it, we can't log out.

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:57.900
That's right.  And there are two of them.

00:06:57.900 --> 00:07:00.010
That program's only for one.

00:07:00.010 --> 00:07:01.580
But you have yours.

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:03.200
You must be joking.

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:06.720
Our mission isn't to rescue the research team.

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:11.010
It's to find the Ignis that created this area and learn their intentions.

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:13.000
I know.

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:16.510
But saving these lives is priority!

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:25.120
A pro treasure hunter needs the courage to know when to retreat.

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:27.860
So willingly giving up the escape program-

00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:30.520
We have no choice!  It's an emergency!

00:07:31.420 --> 00:07:33.620
There's no use talking to you.

00:07:35.560 --> 00:07:41.110
Recent events taught me that I'm still a child.

00:07:43.370 --> 00:07:46.560
I did it for my brother, but look how it turned out.

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:51.250
I troubled everyone, and they needed to save me.

00:07:53.730 --> 00:07:57.710
I was full of myself, thinking I can do anything on my own.

00:07:57.710 --> 00:08:02.940
But in truth, the world is full of people, and we're all connected.

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:06.650
Everyone saved me.

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:09.490
So this time, I want to save everyone.

00:08:09.490 --> 00:08:11.510
I'll become stronger.

00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:16.830
So I decided I'll do everything I possibly can!

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:20.040
But still...

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:28.640
Thank you!

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:49.480
Sheesh.

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:53.080
We have to find a way to escape too.

00:08:53.080 --> 00:08:56.550
What are you talking about?  That's for later.

00:08:58.200 --> 00:08:59.490
Manager Zaizen!

00:08:59.490 --> 00:09:04.040
We just received word that the research team has regained consciousness!

00:09:04.370 --> 00:09:05.600
I see.

00:09:06.030 --> 00:09:08.590
She used the logout program.

00:09:09.080 --> 00:09:11.600
I decided to trust Aoi.

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:18.020
They'll return with a lead on what's happening.

00:09:20.380 --> 00:09:24.210
We've come too far to go home without learning anything.

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:31.090
With my treasure hunter's pride on the line, I'll fulfill this mission!

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:32.160
Understood!

00:09:45.340 --> 00:09:46.930
Not good!

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:49.940
I'm at my limits too!

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:51.100
This is bad.

00:09:51.100 --> 00:09:53.680
We'll be caught in the storm again?

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:59.140
Sorry!  That's all I had!

00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:05.980
The wind...

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:14.340
It stopped blocking us?

00:10:25.660 --> 00:10:27.270
What's that?

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:29.960
There's something there.

00:10:51.320 --> 00:10:52.850
It's quiet.

00:10:52.850 --> 00:10:55.100
Yeah.  Too quiet.

00:11:04.030 --> 00:11:05.200
Someone's here!

00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:17.760
This monster is...

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:26.930
The monster that destroyed Cyberse World!

00:11:27.220 --> 00:11:28.280
What?

00:11:28.280 --> 00:11:29.170
This guy?

00:11:40.040 --> 00:11:42.700
I tricked you!

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:43.750
I'm so happy!

00:11:43.750 --> 00:11:45.720
You were okay?

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:47.200
Yeah.

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:49.200
Ai, is that your friend?

00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:51.370
It's the wind Ignis.

00:11:51.370 --> 00:11:54.560
Yes.  I'm the wind Ignis.

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:56.800
Echo, you can come back.

00:12:04.350 --> 00:12:07.280
Well?  Was my Ignis joke funny?

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:09.650
You went too far!

00:12:09.650 --> 00:12:12.880
Flame was so scared that he farted!

00:12:12.880 --> 00:12:14.740
No, that was you.

00:12:14.740 --> 00:12:17.750
Fart?  Just because of this?

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:22.130
You've hung out with humans for too long that your senses are out of whack.

00:12:22.130 --> 00:12:26.730
Shouldn't you be looking for your Lost Incident partner?

00:12:26.940 --> 00:12:31.240
I can't trust humans like you do.

00:12:31.460 --> 00:12:34.340
I don't want to be captured.

00:12:35.380 --> 00:12:36.810
You're no fun.

00:12:37.080 --> 00:12:40.770
Wind Ignis, did you create this world?

00:12:41.120 --> 00:12:43.040
Wind Ignis...

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:46.240
That name is a bit lacking.

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:51.520
But the Ignis' real names are too hard for humans.

00:12:52.310 --> 00:12:55.140
But I don't want a weird name...

00:12:55.140 --> 00:12:57.390
So call me Windy!

00:12:57.600 --> 00:12:59.120
Windy?

00:12:59.340 --> 00:13:02.700
This is Echo.  A program I created.

00:13:02.940 --> 00:13:07.000
I'm Echo.  A program created by Windy.

00:13:07.280 --> 00:13:10.470
Windy, what are you doing here?

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:13.770
So you're Playmaker.

00:13:13.770 --> 00:13:16.340
The hero who saved LINK VRAINS.

00:13:16.780 --> 00:13:19.580
And the other is Soulburner.

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:25.100
No point standing around talking here.

00:13:25.100 --> 00:13:26.310
Follow me.

00:13:35.030 --> 00:13:40.540
Windy, I'm glad you're okay, but answer that question.

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:42.810
We're in a hurry.

00:13:42.810 --> 00:13:46.080
About why I created this world?

00:13:46.080 --> 00:13:49.100
And what I'm doing here?

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:53.850
For the first question, I was waiting for my friends to show up.

00:13:54.800 --> 00:13:56.500
You were waiting for us?

00:13:56.500 --> 00:13:57.540
Yeah.

00:13:57.950 --> 00:14:00.950
If I connected a world of wind to LINK VRAINS...

00:14:00.950 --> 00:14:05.130
...I thought you'd eventually sniff it out and come here.

00:14:05.130 --> 00:14:06.700
I see.

00:14:07.120 --> 00:14:10.150
Sure enough, you came.

00:14:10.150 --> 00:14:15.030
If we're all together, we can rebuild Cyberse World.

00:14:15.030 --> 00:14:17.400
Rebuild Cyberse World...

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:18.870
Not a bad idea.

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:22.310
Secondly, I wanted to lure the enemy here.

00:14:22.310 --> 00:14:28.850
If you can sniff this place out, the one who destroyed Cyberse World will too.

00:14:29.080 --> 00:14:31.850
What'll you do after luring the enemy?

00:14:31.850 --> 00:14:33.840
Fight 'em, of course.

00:14:33.840 --> 00:14:37.860
They must atone for destroying Cyberse World.

00:14:37.860 --> 00:14:42.460
Even I - who's always calm and collected - feels resentment.

00:14:42.680 --> 00:14:45.910
I didn't know you had such passion.

00:14:46.520 --> 00:14:50.940
I do.  It's just harder to tell than you.

00:14:50.940 --> 00:14:52.820
But you'll fight?

00:14:52.820 --> 00:14:55.040
You've never been that strong.

00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:57.540
That's why I created this world.

00:14:57.540 --> 00:15:02.100
Strong winds created from Data Material make this place a trap.

00:15:02.100 --> 00:15:06.790
I control Data Material better than anyone.

00:15:06.790 --> 00:15:14.580
But it did take time to gather the Data Material scattered throughout the network.

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:17.770
That's why this world only appeared now.

00:15:17.980 --> 00:15:19.130
Exactly.

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:22.820
Windy, we're after someone.

00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:25.140
His name is Bohman.

00:15:25.140 --> 00:15:28.570
He stole my acquaintance's brother's consciousness data.

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:32.380
If we don't retrieve it, he'll be asleep forever.

00:15:32.600 --> 00:15:37.750
He had the same card as the one who destroyed Cyberse World.

00:15:38.770 --> 00:15:40.480
That's very interesting.

00:15:40.760 --> 00:15:42.490
But I don't know.

00:15:42.490 --> 00:15:47.090
Seriously?  He fled into this world.

00:15:47.320 --> 00:15:49.020
You didn't notice?

00:15:49.020 --> 00:15:54.910
Lots of people come here, but most of them self-destruct to the trap.

00:15:54.910 --> 00:15:56.900
My security's perfect.

00:15:56.900 --> 00:15:59.110
I can't watch every little thing-

00:15:59.110 --> 00:16:04.950
Wait a sec.  I once sensed a strange presence at the edge of this world.

00:16:05.370 --> 00:16:06.680
That's it!

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:12.180
Is there a chance that someone created a new world by going through this world?

00:16:12.180 --> 00:16:15.690
And use my trap as a cover?

00:16:15.690 --> 00:16:17.190
That's smart.

00:16:17.190 --> 00:16:18.790
Smart.

00:16:19.470 --> 00:16:21.790
Will you help us?

00:16:21.790 --> 00:16:25.170
Please, Windy.  For my sake.

00:16:34.840 --> 00:16:35.620
I refuse.

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:37.410
You're refusing?

00:16:37.690 --> 00:16:40.710
You said your target came here.

00:16:40.710 --> 00:16:43.650
And that they created a new world.

00:16:43.650 --> 00:16:47.140
But those are only assumptions.

00:16:47.140 --> 00:16:52.160
If you want my help, you need to bring evidence.

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:58.740
But forget that and live here instead.

00:16:58.740 --> 00:17:06.740
Instead of helping humans, we can rebuild Cyberse World quicker if the Ignis come together.

00:17:07.140 --> 00:17:08.210
Well...

00:17:08.210 --> 00:17:12.800
It's true that the Ignis wish to rebuild Cyberse World.

00:17:12.800 --> 00:17:13.810
Flame...

00:17:14.290 --> 00:17:15.180
Right?

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:17.270
But I'll pursue the culprit.

00:17:17.270 --> 00:17:21.190
I want to know the truth about Cyberse World's destruction.

00:17:22.310 --> 00:17:25.160
I feel the same for now.

00:17:26.290 --> 00:17:28.530
So I'm being premature.

00:17:28.530 --> 00:17:29.940
That's right.

00:17:29.940 --> 00:17:34.640
We'll uncover the whole truth and rebuild Cyberse World.

00:17:35.010 --> 00:17:39.940
I see.  I'm just happy to know you're okay.

00:17:39.940 --> 00:17:42.820
So I'll help a little.

00:17:42.820 --> 00:17:45.850
I'll weaken the Data Storm leading to that area.

00:17:46.140 --> 00:17:50.310
That's plenty.  We'll do the rest on our own.

00:17:50.640 --> 00:17:52.780
But I have one condition.

00:17:53.020 --> 00:17:54.890
What condition?

00:17:55.100 --> 00:17:57.250
Do something about them!

00:18:00.190 --> 00:18:01.460
Ghost Girl!

00:18:01.460 --> 00:18:03.230
Who's the other?

00:18:03.230 --> 00:18:05.990
They're tougher than I thought.

00:18:05.990 --> 00:18:08.730
I think they'll make it here.

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:10.340
Can you chase them away?

00:18:10.340 --> 00:18:14.430
If you defeat them in a duel, they'll be ejected from this world.

00:18:14.430 --> 00:18:16.280
Do it yourself.

00:18:16.280 --> 00:18:22.040
No way!  I don't want to reveal myself, and I don't want to risk putting myself in danger.

00:18:22.040 --> 00:18:23.930
You're very cautious.

00:18:23.930 --> 00:18:26.610
Weaken the winds around them.

00:18:26.610 --> 00:18:29.090
If you do, we'll take care of them.

00:18:29.090 --> 00:18:30.430
Hey!

00:18:30.430 --> 00:18:34.490
We fought the Hanoi together, so I'm on good terms with Ghost Girl.

00:18:34.490 --> 00:18:36.530
We can talk and work it out.

00:18:36.960 --> 00:18:38.940
Negotiations complete.

00:18:47.600 --> 00:18:49.320
The wind died down.

00:18:49.640 --> 00:18:50.440
That's...

00:18:51.510 --> 00:18:52.580
Playmaker!

00:18:57.980 --> 00:19:00.090
Long time no see, Playmaker.

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:01.550
Long time no see?

00:19:01.760 --> 00:19:06.020
I owe you for the Tower of Hanoi, but I'll pay you back someday.

00:19:06.240 --> 00:19:08.610
No way!  Are you Blue Angel?

00:19:08.610 --> 00:19:12.400
Really?  You seem pretty different.

00:19:12.400 --> 00:19:15.640
But your new avatar is cool!

00:19:15.640 --> 00:19:17.860
Maybe I'll change my avatar too.

00:19:17.860 --> 00:19:21.410
What's the point?  No one knows you.

00:19:22.110 --> 00:19:24.200
So you're Soulburner.

00:19:24.200 --> 00:19:27.690
Seems we're unexpectedly famous.

00:19:27.690 --> 00:19:30.710
I'm the fire Ignis, Flame.

00:19:30.710 --> 00:19:33.180
So you're also a victim of the Lost Incident?

00:19:33.520 --> 00:19:34.890
Yes.

00:19:35.140 --> 00:19:38.840
The Knights of Hanoi - who caused the Lost Incident - are gone.

00:19:38.840 --> 00:19:43.500
So why are two people with Ignis teaming up?

00:19:44.010 --> 00:19:47.610
We only want to retrieve stolen consciousness data.

00:19:47.940 --> 00:19:49.470
Consciousness data...

00:19:53.660 --> 00:19:55.610
That means he's...

00:19:55.940 --> 00:19:58.880
Why are you here?

00:19:58.880 --> 00:20:01.750
You're gonna use us again, aren't you.

00:20:02.040 --> 00:20:05.710
Yeah.  No point hiding it, so I'll tell you.

00:20:05.710 --> 00:20:08.470
We came to find the Ignis.

00:20:08.470 --> 00:20:10.020
For SOL Technologies?

00:20:10.020 --> 00:20:11.200
Yeah.

00:20:11.200 --> 00:20:16.050
So SOL Technologies didn't only hire rough-looking hunters.

00:20:16.050 --> 00:20:18.960
Didn't expect to see such beauties?

00:20:19.180 --> 00:20:21.570
Never said you were beauties.

00:20:21.570 --> 00:20:24.570
Seems Ignis aren't attracted to me.

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:29.670
SOL-  I mean, my brother can help you.

00:20:29.900 --> 00:20:31.560
You don't understand.

00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:36.380
The Lost Incident made us suffer for a long time.

00:20:36.380 --> 00:20:39.220
SOL Technologies was also responsible for that.

00:20:39.220 --> 00:20:41.850
Entrust our future to them?

00:20:42.100 --> 00:20:43.600
Not a chance.

00:20:43.600 --> 00:20:47.830
Thanks for willing to help, but we'll solve our own problems.

00:20:48.320 --> 00:20:53.170
In that case, those Ignis were originally under SOL Technologies' control.

00:20:53.170 --> 00:20:54.570
Give them back.

00:20:55.320 --> 00:20:56.930
That's crazy.

00:20:56.930 --> 00:20:58.310
Blue Girl!

00:20:58.990 --> 00:21:03.840
If we get their Ignis, we may learn the other Ignis' location.

00:21:04.040 --> 00:21:06.940
If you won't accept our help...

00:21:07.180 --> 00:21:09.680
You'll settle this in a duel?

00:21:09.680 --> 00:21:10.650
That's right!

00:21:11.860 --> 00:21:14.390
There you go, Playmaker.

00:21:15.200 --> 00:21:17.350
They're really eager to duel.

00:21:17.650 --> 00:21:22.930
It's not often that I get to duel Blue Girl, LINK VRAINS's savior.

00:21:22.930 --> 00:21:25.550
It's not bad to gain experience.

00:21:25.550 --> 00:21:27.460
If you win, that is.

00:21:27.880 --> 00:21:30.440
Soulburner, I leave this to you.

00:21:31.570 --> 00:21:33.070
Wait, Playmaker!

00:21:33.070 --> 00:21:34.320
See ya!

00:21:41.480 --> 00:21:43.990
Was this really okay?

00:21:46.900 --> 00:21:52.160
Just like Playmaker, dueling was my life.

